-- title:
--   The column antisymmetrizer maps the row-tabloid module into the line of the polytabloid
-- statement:
--   Let $\mu$ be a Young diagram with $d$ rows, $n\in\mathbb{N}$, and $t$ a tableau of shape $\mu$ (a bijection from the positions $[n]=\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ to the cells of $\mu$). In the word space $W_{n,d}$ of functions on words $[n]\to[d]$, on which $S_n$ acts by $(g\cdot x)(a)=x(a\circ g)$, let $r_t$ be the row word of $t$ ($r_t(p)$ is the row of $t(p)$), and let
--   $$M^t=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{C}}\{\,g\cdot e_{r_t}: g\in S_n\,\}$$
--   be the cyclic subrepresentation generated by $e_{r_t}$, i.e. the row-tabloid permutation module spanned by the basis vectors of all rearrangements of $r_t$. With $A_t=\sum_{g\in C_t}\operatorname{sgn}(g)\,g$ the column antisymmetrizer of $t$ ($C_t$ the column group) and $e_t=A_te_{r_t}$ the polytabloid, the theorem states
--   $$A_t\,x\in\mathbb{C}\,e_t\qquad\text{for every }x\in M^t .$$
--
--   Since the Specht module of $t$ is contained in $M^t$, this rank-one property is what makes every nonzero vector of the Specht module generate the whole module, and hence what makes the Specht module irreducible.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $M^t$ is `tabloidSub t`, the cyclic subrepresentation generated by `Pi.single (rowWord t) 1`; the conclusion is membership in `Submodule.span ℂ {polytabloid t}`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/RepresentationTheory/Saxl/SpechtSubmodule.lean#L52-L66

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_Saxl
import Definitions.Def_OAI_RepresentationTheory_Saxl_Basic
import Definitions.Def_OAI_RepresentationTheory_Saxl_Polytabloid
import Definitions.Def_OAI_RepresentationTheory_Saxl_SpechtSubmodule

open OAI OAI.Saxl
open scoped TensorProduct
universe uG uV

theorem OAI.Saxl.columnAlt_tabloid {n : ℕ} {μ : YoungDiagram} (t : Tableau n μ)
    {x : WordSpace n (μ.colLen 0)} (hx : x ∈ tabloidSub t) :
    columnAlt t x ∈ Submodule.span ℂ {polytabloid t} := by sorry
